    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d719">

                <pb facs="0793" n="781" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg781"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 P.W./11–2344</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Halifax</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stettinius</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-23">November 23,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Ed</hi>: I send you herewith an <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Aide-Mémoire</hi> concerning proposals for the use of
                    the French in pre-operational activities in Indo-China.</p>
                <p>This is a matter which Mountbatten and all of us have very much at heart. Until
                    we have the all-clear from your side he cannot effectively carry out sabotage
                    etc. activities which he is satisfied should contribute very considerably to his
                    task.</p>
                <p>You will see that the matter is urgent and I would be grateful if you could let
                    us have a very early reply.</p>
                <p>V. sin[cerely,]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Halifax</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d719-a1.xml" xpointer="d719-a1"/>
            </div>
